 "_looks": "look: what the close-up shows. jet / companion (a star it pulls gas from) / crowd (dense stars around it) / ring / pulsar / dim (fainter clouds) / irregular / tilt (degrees, as we see it) / squash (how flat its sky picture is).",
 "_planetExtras": "Optional planet fields: eqRKm, polRKm (km, equator and pole radius), tiltDeg (spin axis tilt), rings (edges in km from the centre: C0 inner edge, C1/B1/A0 ring boundaries, A1 outer edge), moons [{name, aKm orbit radius, rKm body radius, col 0..1, look, haze, major, side}], side (which way the name tag points: [right=1/left=-1, down=1/up=-1]). Saturn: NASA Saturn and Saturnian satellite fact sheets; ring edges: PDS Rings Node. Earth, Moon, Jupiter and its four large moons: NASA NSSDC fact sheets (Earth/Jupiter/Moon/Jovian satellites), checked 2026-11-23. Moon colours and looks are artistic. cls: the planet's class when its size alone would put it in the wrong one (rocky, subneptune, neptune, giant).",
 "_time": "ONE time model (see the catalogue script): every orbiting body's place is worked out for today's date. Our planets: real, from `orbit` = JPL 'Approximate Positions of the Planets' Table 1 (a, e, I, L, long.peri, long.node, then their rates per century; Earth uses the Earth-Moon barycentre row). Moons: real orbit periods (`perDays`, NASA NSSDC satellite fact sheets) but an INVENTED starting point. Other stars' planets: real periods where the archive has them, INVENTED starting point."
}